================================================================================
What citation requirements apply to SliceBench results in a paper / model card
================================================================================

If you report a SliceBench score in a publication or model card, cite:

  1. Each dataset whose brains are included in the bench tier you used.
     See per-dataset NOTICE files for the exact citation format.

  2. The SliceBench code repository itself (as the benchmark methodology
     source). Use the repo URL + the version / commit SHA you ran against.

================================================================================
Commercial-use status
================================================================================

While SliceBench includes Allen-sourced brains (allen_connectivity,
allen_dev_coronal, and the ISH_Calb1 brain inside deepslice_gt), the
bench-as-distributed inherits the most-restrictive license:
**noncommercial research use only**. The SliceBench CODE under MIT is
unrestricted; the bundled DATA is bound by each dataset's terms.

To produce a fully commercial-OK version, drop Allen-sourced content
(allen_connectivity, allen_dev_coronal, and the ISH_Calb1 subject from
deepslice_gt) and re-publish; the remaining CC BY 4.0 sources cover both
academic and commercial use with attribution.

For the Gemma 4 Good open-source academic hackathon (Kaggle prize
eligibility, fully open-source model + benchmark): the bench is being
published for noncommercial research use, which falls under the permission
grant in every included dataset's license. See LICENSES_CORONAL.md for
the per-dataset reasoning.
